{#
A settings section card.

Twenty-two sections hand-rolled this shape and only three finished the job, so
the page was a mix of real cards, headings with a bordered box under them, and
bare content sitting flush against the pane edge. This is that shape, once.

EMBED, not include or macro, because two sections need markup inside the header
(Accounts' "Add account" button) and every section needs markup in the body.
A macro pair can open a header but cannot let the caller put anything in it.

    {% embed 'settings/_card.html.twig' with {
        heading:    'settings.labels.heading'|trans,
        subheading: 'settings.labels.subheading'|trans,
    } %}
        {% block body %}…{% endblock %}
    {% endembed %}

Params:
    heading     required, already translated
    subheading  optional, already translated
    padded      body gets its own inset — see chrome.body(); default false,
                because most bodies are lists that pad their own rows
    class       extra classes on the <section>, for margins at the call site

Blocks:
    body        the card's content
    actions     optional control at the right of the header band

The heading is an <h2> and there is exactly one per card, so a section of four
cards is four h2s at the same level rather than a nest. Groups INSIDE a body
use h3.

Not interactive and must not look it: no tabindex, no role, no aria-expanded.
Admin panels collapse and carry those; a settings card is a surface, not a
control. Both draw their chrome from _partials/_card_chrome.html.twig.
#}
{% import '_partials/_card_chrome.html.twig' as chrome %}

<section class="{{ chrome.shell() }}{{ class|default('') ? ' ' ~ class|default('') : '' }}">
    <header class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3 {{ chrome.band() }}">
        <div class="min-w-0">
            <h2 class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink">{{ heading }}</h2>
            {% if subheading|default(null) %}
                <p class="text-xs text-ink-faint mt-0.5">{{ subheading }}</p>
            {% endif %}
        </div>

        {% block actions %}{% endblock %}
    </header>

    <div class="{{ padded|default(false) ? chrome.body() : '' }}">
        {% block body %}{% endblock %}
    </div>
</section>
